From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:06:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vm: inline hottest opcodes in Context::run with cached pc,
 rp, and bytecode

In WebAssembly every OPCODE_HANDLERS[op] dispatch is a call_indirect with
signature checks, ABI overhead, and a ControlFlow<CompletionRecord> return,
plus reloading frame, pc, rp, and bytecode slice on every instruction.

Inline the hottest non-frame-changing opcodes (register moves, jumps,
constant stores, int32 arithmetic/bitwise/comparison fast paths, and loop
iteration checks) in a br_table loop inside Context::run, syncing pc and
reloading frame state only on fallback to OPCODE_HANDLERS.
